# configure/cloud-sync.md: the cloud rows on GAME SETTINGS, the cloud hub,
# the tick page behind BACK UP TO THE CLOUD, and CONNECT OR REPAIR CLOUD
# STORAGE. GAME SETTINGS is twelve presses up from the MAIN MENU's top row
# (the unmarked stop, BACK, QUIT, then nine rows); it opens on its first row, and up wraps
# through BACK and PER SYSTEM ADVANCED CONFIGURATION to MANAGE CLOUD
# STORAGE, the last row of the CLOUD SETTINGS group. On the hub, BACK UP TO
# THE CLOUD is the first row and CONNECT OR REPAIR CLOUD STORAGE the eighth
# press down (CONNECTED TO is a focus stop).
# The MAIN MENU is reached from its bottom, so the walk is the same whether
# the guest is signed in to RetroAchievements (the menu then opens on that
# row, above GAME SETTINGS) or not. Probed one press at a time on 2026-09-29
# (proofs-307/up-probe.steps): up from the top row lands on an unmarked stop
# with nothing highlighted, the next on BACK, the third on QUIT, and the rows
# above QUIT never move. Three presses to QUIT, not two.
key ret
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
